-- title:
--   An element of density at least $3/8$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=6$ of the scaled union-closed sets conjecture.** Every finite union-closed family $\mathcal F$ of finite sets with $\mathcal F\ne\emptyset$ and $\mathcal F\ne\{\emptyset\}$ has an element of density at least $\tfrac12-\tfrac18$:
--
--   $$\exists x:\quad \delta_{\mathcal F}(x)\ \ge\ \frac38 .$$
-- source:
--   Z. Chase, S. Lovett, Approximate union closed conjecture, https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.11689, Theorem 1 (density at least $\frac{3-\sqrt5}{2}$); independently W. Sawin, https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.11504, R. Alweiss, B. Huang, M. Sellke, https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.11731, L. Pebody, https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.13139

